                <pb facs="1039" n="919" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg919"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bowen to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-06-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen reports that the manager of the Bermudez Company informs him that the
                    Venezuelan Government threatens suit unless the company pay $10,000,000 to the
                    Venezuelan Government. He advised him to pay nothing, to defend their rights in
                    court, and to publish facts; thinks the company’s policy should be honest and
                    fearless.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
